on updates.\n+- If one or more ORCID are provided for a new term, these MUST be added as Dublin Core Terms contributor axioms, e.g. `AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0000118 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2825-0621>)`. Do not add contributor annotations when editing existing terms.\n \n ```\n # Class: obo:CL_4072102 (Purkinje layer interneuron)\n@@ -92,6 +99,7 @@ EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4072102 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeV\n SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072102 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\n ```\n \n+\n No relationship should point to an obsolete term - when you obsolete a term, you may need to also rewire\n terms to \"skip\" the obsoleted term.\n \n@@ -99,7 +107,8 @@ terms to \"skip\" the obsoleted term.\n \n - Link back to the issue you are dealing with using the `term_tracker_item`\n - All terms should have definitions, with at least one definition xref, ideally a PMID\n-- You can sign terms as `created_by: dragon-ai-agent`\n+- You can sign terms as `dc:creator \"GitHub Copilot\"` only when creating new terms. Do not add `dc:creator` when editing existing terms, including textual definition updates.\n+\n \n ## Relationships\n \n@@ -121,4 +130,3 @@ SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072102 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\n ```\n \n The reasoner can find the most specific `is_a`, so it's OK to leave this off.\n-\n","exit":0,"description":"Shows diff for edited guidance files","truncated":false},"title":"Shows diff for edited guidance files","time":{"start":1778977474399,"end":1778977474405}},"id":"prt_e335206ea001e5WRHbfU1UzXwI","sessionID":"ses_1ccaede7cffe5Jxx9jj6XWQS7c","messageID":"msg_e3351efb7001N2n5457mWl6W1v"}}
